  "id": "topographical-disorientation",
  "term": "topographical disorientation",
  "definition": "Topographical disorientation is a problem with spatial navigation, in which a person has marked difficulty finding their way in the environment. In the source, it is described as occurring after brain damage and being associated with impaired topographical skills.",
